From 53878b37b2156e8884f3fb8baf720eade9ae755a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lucascouts <lucascs@protonmail.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 15:19:58 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] agent_ui: a Run button sends a recommended slash command in a
 new thread

0045 put a New Thread button beside Copy on a code block that holds one slash
command: it opens a new thread with the same agent and the command in the
composer, unsent. Most of the time the command is exactly what the operator
wants, and the click is followed by Enter. A Run button now sits left of it
and does both at once: it opens the thread and sends the command (story 035,
R1). New Thread keeps its prefill-only behaviour.

**Run sends only what the clicked block shows.** On click, Run re-reads
`slash_command_in_code_block` from the code the click hands over, never from
the message, so with two qualifying blocks each Run sends its own block's
trimmed command. Run exists only where New Thread does -- an agent message,
one non-empty line starting with `/` -- with Copy's visibility, and never on
thinking blocks, tool output, user messages or the composer preview.

**Several actions per code block.** `MarkdownElement::on_code_block_action`
now takes `impl Fn(&str) -> Vec<CodeBlockAction>`: every returned action is
drawn in list order before Copy, and an empty list draws nothing, as `None`
did. Each button's element id carries the action's index
(`("code-block-action", markdown_id)` / `"<range.end>-<index>"`), so two
actions of one block and the actions of neighbouring blocks never share an
id. `slash_command_action` returns `[Run, New Thread]`; the row reads
[Run] [New Thread] [Copy]. Run is a focusable `IconButton`
(`IconName::PlayOutlined`, tooltip "Run in New Thread").

**Opening and sending.** `AgentPanel::run_prompt_in_new_thread(agent,
source_session, text)` sits above `new_thread_with_prefilled_prompt`, and both
share `ensure_agent_available`: an agent that is no longer configured opens
nothing, sends nothing and shows 0045's toast, logged at WARN with the agent
id and the source session. A successful Run logs one INFO line, `action=run`,
with the agent id, the source session and the command's length -- never its
text. The source thread is left unchanged and still listed.

**Run's first message skips the slash-command check, and nothing else does.**
`MessageEditor::contents` refuses a leading `/name` that is not in the agent's
advertised commands or skills. A brand-new thread has advertised none: the
adapter sends `available_commands_update` only after `newSession` returns. So
reusing `ContentBlock { auto_submit: true }` refused every Run ("not a
recognized command ... Available commands: none"). Run therefore opens the
thread with a new `AgentInitialContent::RunCommand { blocks }`, which
`ThreadView::new` auto-submits with `MessageEditor::skip_slash_command_check`
set around that single `send()` and cleared right after. The composer, the
new-thread button's prefill once sent, the git panel's review and conflict
actions, the `create_thread` tool and the `?prompt=` deep link (which never
auto-submits) keep the check; `validate_slash_commands` is unchanged.

Tests: 8 markdown tests for the list-shaped hook (replacing 0045's 6), 4
panel tests for Run (same agent, sent once, verbatim, unavailable agent, the
prefill path still unsent), 8 for the one-shot skip (Run sends an unadvertised
command; the composer, a prefilled send, another auto-submit, the URL deep
link, a second command after Run and threads opened after Run are all still
refused) and 5 GPUI tests that sweep the panel for Run and click it.

Pure Zed and generic ACP: it rides `claude-agent-acp-plus` BY CHOICE, like
0043 and 0045, and needs no adapter feature.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---

